        "dependency_level": 3,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "statement": "Let $H=\\mathbb Ce$ with $\\|e\\|=1$, and write $|n\\rangle=e^{\\otimes n}$\nfor its normalized bosonic $n$-particle vector, including $|0\\rangle=\\Omega$.\nOn the one-mode fermionic Fock space write $|1\\rangle=c^\\dagger(e)\\Omega$.\nThe one-mode bosonic and fermionic operators satisfy the CCR and CAR on their\nstated domains. The bosonic number operator from\n[[lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum]] is\n$N|n\\rangle=n|n\\rangle$ with\n$$D(N)=\\left\\{(c_n)_{n\\ge0}:\\sum_{n\\ge0}n^2|c_n|^2<\\infty\\right\\}.$$\nThe Fock vector\n$$\\Psi=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}(n+1)^{-3/2}|n\\rangle$$\nbelongs to $D(a(e))\\cap D(a^\\dagger(e))$ but not to $D(N)$.",
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Jan Dereziński, Mathematical Introduction to Quantum Field Theory, §§5.4–5.5",
              "url": "https://www.fuw.edu.pl/~derezins/qft-lectures.pdf",
              "locator": "Full 136-page author-hosted notes; creation, annihilation and Fock sectors, PDF pp. 35–37."
            },
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, §2.4",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qft.pdf",
              "locator": "Complete 155-page author-hosted notes; number operator and multiparticle Fock states, printed pp. 29–30."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
